[thin] Specific flexure: the cap's two spring wings are 1.5 mm thick from the round end of each wing gap to their tips, the anchor cap's wing. Everything else in the cap is the solid saddle round the bore, 2.75 mm, which keeps 2.5 mm past the bore's mouth ease.
alternatives: A thicker wing strains more going on, past the faucet display cover's on the same beam estimate. Filling the gap stiffens the wing's root, which then takes the whole bend over a shorter length.
